        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Harmonize dragover event timing with the HTML spec]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45235</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45235"/>
        <updated>2026-08-19T07:14:46.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186379818?u=4fa416d9a926677b033c0b52ba207d6cf7cd7920&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Corrects the <code class="notranslate">dragover</code> timing description:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><code class="notranslate">DragEvent</code> page previously claimed dragover fires "every 50 ms, else 5ms/1ms"; this now states the spec value (every 350 ms ± 200 ms, per the HTML spec) with a link to the spec.</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">HTMLElement/dragover_event</code> now states the same spec value.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Multiple MDN pages described <code class="notranslate">dragover</code> timing inconsistently and one value contradicted the WHATWG spec. This resolves the inconsistency as described in the linked issue.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #36689.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2641972922" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/36689" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/36689/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/36689">#36689</a></p>]]></content>
