        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Clarify that switching applications does not always exit fullscreen]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45234</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45234"/>
        <updated>2026-08-19T07:14:35.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186379818?u=4fa416d9a926677b033c0b52ba207d6cf7cd7920&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Caveats the previous statement that switching applications with Alt+Tab always exits fullscreen. Notes that in multi-monitor setups, or on platforms where fullscreen runs as its own space (such as macOS), switching apps may not exit fullscreen, and that Esc/F11 reliably exit fullscreen.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The previous wording was inaccurate in multi-desktop environments (see linked issue).</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
