        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add overflow: clip guidance and recommend auto over scroll]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45232</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45232"/>
        <updated>2026-08-19T08:13:58.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186379818?u=4fa416d9a926677b033c0b52ba207d6cf7cd7920&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Updates the "Overflowing content" guide:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>recommends <code class="notranslate">overflow: auto</code> over <code class="notranslate">scroll</code> for boxes that need to scroll, since <code class="notranslate">auto</code> shows scrollbars only when needed;</li>
<li>adds a "Clipping overflowing content" section explaining <code class="notranslate">overflow: clip</code>, how it differs from <code class="notranslate">hidden</code> (no scroll container, per-axis clipping with <code class="notranslate">visible</code>) and <code class="notranslate">overflow-clip-margin</code>.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The guide previously omitted <code class="notranslate">clip</code> entirely and gave <code class="notranslate">auto</code> only a brief mention. <code class="notranslate">clip</code> and <code class="notranslate">auto</code> are the values many developers should reach for in these cases.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #32173.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2124315378" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32173" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/32173/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32173">#32173</a></p>]]></content>
